        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.166,
            0.819,
            0.399
          ],
          "content": "| Life time (in hours) | Number of lamps |\n| --- | --- |\n| 1500 - 2000 | 14 |\n| 2000 - 2500 | 56 |\n| 2500 - 3000 | 60 |\n| 3000 - 3500 | 86 |\n| 3500 - 4000 | 74 |\n| 4000 - 4500 | 62 |\n| 4500 - 5000 | 48 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_29_table_3.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.41,
            0.459,
            0.428
          ],
          "content": "Find the median life time of a lamp."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.124,
            0.434,
            0.9,
            0.487
          ],
          "content": "**6.** 100 surnames were randomly picked up from a local telephone directory and the frequency distribution of the number of letters in the English alphabets in the surnames was obtained as follows:"
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.489,
            0.896,
            0.562
          ],
          "content": "| Number of letters | 1 - 4 | 4 - 7 | 7 - 10 | 10 - 13 | 13 - 16 | 16 - 19 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of surnames | 6 | 30 | 40 | 16 | 4 | 4 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_29_table_6.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.155,
            0.572,
            0.902,
            0.607
          ],
          "content": "Determine the median number of letters in the surnames. Find the mean number of letters in the surnames? Also, find the modal size of the surnames."
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.612,
            0.901,
            0.648
          ],
          "content": "**7.** The distribution below gives the weights of 30 students of a class. Find the median weight of the students."
        },
        {
          "type": "table",
          "bbox": [
            0.158,
            0.653,
            0.897,
            0.729
          ],
          "content": "| Weight (in kg) | 40 - 45 | 45 - 50 | 50 - 55 | 55 - 60 | 60 - 65 | 65 - 70 | 70 - 75 |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Number of students | 2 | 3 | 8 | 6 | 6 | 3 | 2 |",
          "captions": [],
          "footnotes": [],
          "image_source": "images/page_29_table_9.jpg"
        },
        {
          "type": "paragraph_title",
          "bbox": [
            0.098,
            0.753,
            0.264,
            0.773
          ],
          "level": 2,
          "content": "13.5 Summary"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.097,
            0.779,
            0.572,
            0.798
          ],
          "content": "In this chapter, you have studied the following points:"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.125,
            0.803,
            0.553,
            0.821
          ],
          "content": "**1.** The mean for grouped data can be found by :"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.172,
            0.826,
            0.462,
            0.867
          ],
          "content": "(i) the direct method : $\\overline { { x } } = \\frac { \\Sigma f _ { i } x _ { i } } { \\Sigma f _ { i } }$"
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "bbox": [
            0.167,
            0.87,
            0.578,
            0.908
          ],
          "content": "(ii) the assumed mean method : $\\overline { { x } } = a + \\frac { \\Sigma f _ { i } d _ { i } } { \\Sigma f _ { i } }$"
        },
